# Rank 1589 / CVE-2025-6032: podman machine init inverted its
# TLS-verify option when handing it to the image pull, so the
# default zero value of the bool (TLSVerify=false) produced
# InsecureSkipVerify=true -- every machine-init image pull verified
# no certificates and a network attacker could serve the image
# (certificate validation disabled by inverted default, CWE-295).
# The pull setup in pkg/machine/ocipull/pull.go did
# `DockerInsecureSkipTLSVerify: types.NewOptionalBool(!o.pullOptions.
# TLSVerify)` -- the negation makes the secure-by-default posture
# insecure-by-default. the fixing commit is the fixing change
# (confirmed, "machine init: fix tls check. Ensure we verify the
# TLS connection when pulling the OCI image."): the option becomes
# `SkipTLSVerify types.OptionalBool` (unset means verify) and the
# assignment passes it through without negation. No pool
# correction.
#
# ATTENTION, inverted security defaults. The flag exists and is
# consumed correctly -- the defect is one negation that flips the
# default posture, the default-inversion sibling of rank 1535's
# open-bind and rank 1540's default-open authorization: no rule can
# ask "does the secure option's default compose to a secure
# configuration" -- that is default-posture vocabulary over a
# project-specific option type (types.OptionalBool). A binding on
# podman's own pullOptions would detect this tool rather than the
# weakness. Measured on the real code: scanning pkg/machine/ocipull/
# reports zero findings at both revisions. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry.
# No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1589 records the
# negated flag handoff and the OptionalBool form, both asserting
# reject VYQL-CFG-004: when default-posture vocabulary lands, the
# negated form must flip to expect.

test "rank1589: the verify flag is negated into the pull options"
  lang go
  file pkg/machine/ocipull/pull.go
  reject VYQL-CFG-004
  code
  ```
  package ocipull

  type PullOptions struct {
      // Require HTTPS and verify certificates when accessing the registry.
      TLSVerify bool
  }

  func newDockerOptions(o PullOptions) *dockerOptions {
      return &dockerOptions{
          DockerInsecureSkipTLSVerify: newOptionalBool(!o.TLSVerify),
      }
  }

  type dockerOptions struct {
      DockerInsecureSkipTLSVerify optionalBool
  }

  type optionalBool struct {
      value bool
      set   bool
  }

  func newOptionalBool(v bool) optionalBool {
      return optionalBool{value: v, set: true}
  }
  ```

test "rank1589: the fixed revision passes an explicit skip flag through"
  lang go
  file pkg/machine/ocipull/pull.go
  reject VYQL-CFG-004
  code
  ```
  package ocipull

  type PullOptions struct {
      // Skip TLS verification when accessing the registry.
      SkipTLSVerify optionalBool
  }

  func newDockerOptions(o PullOptions) *dockerOptions {
      return &dockerOptions{
          DockerInsecureSkipTLSVerify: o.SkipTLSVerify,
      }
  }

  type dockerOptions struct {
      DockerInsecureSkipTLSVerify optionalBool
  }

  type optionalBool struct {
      value bool
      set   bool
  }
  ```
